# DevStack Project Rules

Full context is in `AGENTS.md` at the repo root. Read it first.

## Python rules

- All subprocess calls must pass `creationflags=no_window_flags()` from `core/utils.py`
- Never use bare `zipfile.extractall()` — use `safe_extractall()` from `core/utils.py`
- Never store `admin_pass` in any config file or sites.json
- QThread workers: never null the worker reference inside `finished` signal handlers
- Load settings once per worker run: `self._cached_settings = load_settings()` in `run()`
- Use `str | None` union syntax — Python 3.10+ minimum

## UI rules

- Style target: Windows 11 utility (calm, flat, scannable) — see `UI-RULES.md`
- One primary button per group. Secondary = neutral border. Destructive = red fill only.
- Status colors: green=running, amber=partial, red=stopped. Don't flood areas with color.
- `QFont()` takes a single family name — NOT a CSS comma-separated font list
- All spinboxes use `GuardedSpinBox`, all settings comboboxes use `GuardedComboBox`
  (react to scroll only when the mouse is over them)

## Web layer rules

- The web dashboard is READ-ONLY — never add service start/stop controls to it
- `dashboard/api.php` runs `status.ps1` and returns JSON; the portal/dashboard poll it via JS
- Always use `htmlspecialchars()` before echoing any variable into HTML
- Never use `shell_exec()`/`exec()` with unvalidated user input

## Config / portability rules

- Never hardcode absolute paths in nginx.conf / httpd.conf / my.ini — use `DEVSTACK_ROOT` placeholder
- `php.ini` uses relative `extension_dir = "ext"`
- Never add nginx perf directives that hurt localhost (gzip, tcp_nopush, open_file_cache)

## Security rules (already applied — maintain them)

- Zip Slip protection in all extraction paths
- SHA256 verification field exists in PHP version entries (populate from php.net)
- No `--allow-root` in WP-CLI commands
- No `shell=True` in Python subprocess
